/// Behavioral API documentation for the backend.
///
/// This mixin exposes a single static query, `getApiDoc`, that returns a
/// Markdown description of the canister's public API. The document is authored
/// from the current backend source and reads no runtime state.
mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister is a deliberately minimal backend for a client-side medical education web app. All health data — patient records, observations, conditions, medications, allergies, questionnaire responses, Bluetooth readings, and prediction results — is stored only in the user's browser (IndexedDB). The canister accepts, stores, and transmits no health data.\n\nIts only responsibilities are:\n\n- the shared authorization helpers (`assignCallerUserRole`, `getCallerUserRole`, `isCallerAdmin`) provided by the authorization mixin, and\n- the OQL `Expose` mixin, which currently registers **no entities** because the canister persists no queryable application data.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `assignCallerUserRole(user : Principal, role : UserRole) : async ()`\n\nUpdate call. Assigns a role to `user`. Only an existing admin may call it; the first caller to initialize access control becomes the initial admin. Traps for a non-admin caller.\n\n### `getCallerUserRole() : async UserRole`\n\nQuery. Returns the role of the calling principal. An unregistered caller receives the default `#user` role.\n\n### `isCallerAdmin() : async Bool`\n\nQuery. Returns `true` when the calling principal is an admin.\n\n### `_initialize_access_control() : async ()`\n\nUpdate call. Registers the calling principal. The first caller becomes the admin; subsequent callers become regular users. A caller that never signs in through the app's frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the app owner.\n\n### `schema() : async Text`\n\nQuery. Returns the OQL schema as JSON. Because no entities are registered, the schema contains an empty entity list.\n\n### `execute(query : Text) : async Text`\n\nQuery. Runs an OQL JSON query against the registered entities. With no entities registered, every query returns an empty result set.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nQuery. Returns this document.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- `assignCallerUserRole` and `_initialize_access_control` are update calls that require a signed (non-anonymous) caller.\n- `getCallerUserRole`, `isCallerAdmin`, `schema`, `execute`, and `getApiDoc` are queries.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration is a prerequisite for role-guarded calls: a direct API caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call. The first initializer receives the admin role; every later caller receives the regular user role. An unregistered or anonymous caller is rejected on guarded endpoints with a trap.\n- A caller can be unregistered while assuming the app already knows it: registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- Timestamps, where they appear in OQL results, are signed 64-bit nanosecond counts (`Int`).\n- Principals are encoded as text in OQL values and JSON results.\n- Optional values are encoded as JSON `null` when absent.\n- `schema` and `execute` return JSON encoded as `Text`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `schema` and `execute` are queries and complete in a single round trip; no polling is required.\n- `execute` returns a complete result set for the given query; there is no cursor or continuation token.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `_initialize_access_control` is idempotent in effect: calling it again for an already-registered principal does not change that principal's role.\n- `assignCallerUserRole` is idempotent: assigning the same role twice leaves the same state.\n- No method deletes or mutates health data, because no health data is stored on the canister.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Role-guarded calls trap for callers that are not registered or not authorized; the trap message is opaque to the frontend.\n- `execute` never returns an error for an unknown entity; it returns an empty result set.\n- Because the canister stores no application data, OQL queries cannot answer questions about the user's health records — those live only in the browser.\n";
  };
};
